          "source_text_sha256": "88ba73cb0c49c4dd593d6c2314932f87a5a68b02aff44d44d340a2c62a0f432c",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On August 11, 2015, around 10:05 PM, a witness on their terrace was intrigued by two lights of different colors at low altitude that they saw in the clear sky. The lights moved silently in a straight line, then accelerated, zigzagged, and resumed a straight trajectory before disappearing. The lights maintained the same spacing between them during their movement. The witness added to their report their GPS position, the exact azimuth of observation, and a annotated photograph depicting their observation. Only one report was received by GEIPAN. Given the information collected (see the investigation report), namely:\n\n- No data regarding the colors of PAN.\n\nAlthough the most plausible hypothesis (confusion with a night-flying drone) could have been considered, we can say that the lack of information does not allow a definitive conclusion in favor of this hypothesis. GEIPAN classifies this case as \"C,\" as an observation of an unidentified phenomenon at this stage, with a lack of cross-references and elements that do not allow for a solid opinion.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "836fdbe4d971d3da540a6d06f1c83745c4f6853fcf1a27f05a7e1b0d486ae370"
        }
      ],
